Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Ryan-Holiday.md` and appended the `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom. No body edits.

**The two biggest issues I flagged:**

1. **The central contradiction gets resolved instead of held open.** The entity-gap packet's whole thesis is the manipulator-turned-stillness-merchant tension, with an explicit instruction to sit inside it "without pretending to settle it." The draft settles it in one clause — "every book since has been restitution with an ISBN" — and the only counter-pressure (Doug Bates on "brand") lands ~1,500 words later and only rebuts brand defense as a motive for the *video*. The larger question — penance, or the American Apparel engine repointed — never gets asked.

2. **"I'm a good father" is quoted twice and never cashed.** That's the last item in Greene's improvised self-image, and the draft has a Daily Dad newsletter *and* podcast, two sons, and a police-detective-plus-principal household sitting right there. Samantha is never named despite appearing on his own podcast and co-founding the bookstore with him.

Also worth your attention: two verified gaps and one accuracy flag. The NFL adoption is absent entirely (Seahawks *and* Patriots, weeks before Super Bowl XLIX, at 27 — ESPN traced it through the Patriot Way and Nick Saban), The Painted Porch is walked past twice without being named or having its ~750-titles-vs-10,000 curation policy mentioned, and the epigraph is Marcus Aurelius *Meditations* 10.16 with a swear added but is attributed flatly to "Ryan Holiday, April 2026" — readers of *Meditations* will read that as an error.

Body is ~3,957 words against the 4,500 ceiling, so I noted the swim (6 appearances) and Greene (3) trims should come before the additions.

Sources: [ESPN on the NFL adoption](https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/29200293/the-ancient-credo-fueled-patriot-way-inspired-nick-saban-helped-ryan-shazier-heal), [Texas Monthly on the Bastrop bookshop](https://www.texasmonthly.com/arts-entertainment/ryan-holiday-stoic-king-bastrop-painted-porch/), [Austin Monthly on the couple founding it](https://www.austinmonthly.com/despite-a-global-pandemic-and-historic-freeze-this-couple-created-a-thriving-bookstore-in-bastrop/), [Holiday's own Pigliucci interview](https://ryanholiday.net/an-interview-on-stoicism-with-massimo-pigliucci/).
